Make tests independent of workspace path length and installed PHP settings.

The FPM test helper's existing temporary-directory fallback does not help
when TMPDIR itself is a long path.  Use a hashed /tmp socket name as the
final fallback.  Ensure a child PHP process that is deliberately given an
empty environment does not load the build host's installed configuration.
The no-INI child must also omit inherited arguments containing an explicit
-c option.

Allow enough FPM log space to retain the complete fatal-error backtrace
when the source pathname is long; keep the full upstream error assertions.

Will submit upstream.


--- php-8.5.11/ext/standard/tests/file/bug60120.phpt
+++ php-8.5.11/ext/standard/tests/file/bug60120.phpt
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ if (PHP_OS_FAMILY === 'Windows') die('sk
 
 $php = getenv('TEST_PHP_EXECUTABLE_ESCAPED');
 $args = getenv('TEST_PHP_EXTRA_ARGS');
-$cmd = ' -r "\$in = file_get_contents(\'php://stdin\'); fwrite(STDOUT, \$in); fwrite(STDERR, \$in);"';
+$cmd = ' -n -r "\$in = file_get_contents(\'php://stdin\'); fwrite(STDOUT, \$in); fwrite(STDERR, \$in);"';
 $cmd = join(' ', [$php, $args, $cmd]);
 $descriptors = array(array('pipe', 'r'), array('pipe', 'w'), array('pipe', 'w'));
 $stdin = str_repeat('*', 2049 );
